        "id": 1432579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T06:37:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consider putting all required parameters to Builder c-tor. See go/android-api-guidelines#builders-nonnull-constructors",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 410,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 412,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "9a54478e46e14bfd669997826cee0a6a06ce101f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d4f60aa1_a6f6fd3f",
        "filename": "javalib/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachineConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 412,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T07:49:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That says that all constructor parameters must be required, but not that all required parameters must be constructor parameters.\n\nI want to make this really explicit - one mistake one of our clients made was not to ask for protected. And new Builder(ctx).setProtected(false) seems a lot harder to do accidentally than new Builder(ctx, false).",
      "parentUuid": "de8b5b01_84b5d5bc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 410,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 412,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "9a54478e46e14bfd669997826cee0a6a06ce101f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b777cde1_16d9efc5",
        "filename": "javalib/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachineConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 412,
      "author": {
        "id": 1432579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T12:13:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general compile time checks that client specifies a required value are preferred over the runtime ones, but I see your point about the the context that setProtected() name gives. The current approach SGTM, we can discuss alternatives in the @SystemApi change (again, need to think a little bit more)",
      "parentUuid": "d4f60aa1_a6f6fd3f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 410,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 412,
        "endChar": 34
